Ollama (Download and run large language models locally)

Ollama is an application which lets you run large language models
offline.

A list of models are available on ollama.com/library.

Optional dependencies, namely CUDA, ROCm and Vulkan, will be
automatically detected by the script.

To disable CUDA accelerators, use CUDA=OFF.

To disable HIP accelerators, use ROCM=OFF.

If you have vulkan-sdk>=1.4, Vulkan accelerators will be built. To
disable them, use VULKAN=OFF.

If you use Sapphire Rapids CPU backend, you may need to install GCC 15
from testing/ first to avoid segfaults due to GCC 11 building broken
AMX code.

Optional dependencies:
- cudatoolkit_13 - for CUDA accelerators
- rocmtoolkit_7 - for HIP accelerators
